<title>RUSSIA: Price of Russian 504-day bond tranche 100.35.</title>
<headline>Price of Russian 504-day bond tranche 100.35.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price of a new Russian 504-day OFZ interest-bearing bond tranche amounted to 100.35 percent at auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>The issue closed at 100.10 to yield 35.58 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Dealers forecast the average price would be in a 99.73-100.20 percent range.</p>
<p>    Series number		24010 (additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	     3.34 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	     1.52 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		     1.59 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	    100.35 trln</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price  100.35 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	     35.12 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield  35.12 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	  504 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		   Jan 29, 1997</p>
<p>    Original issue date	Dec 18, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity		     June 17, 1998</p>
<p>On January 29 the finance ministry repaid about 6.63 trillion roubles of maturing six-month T-bills (series 22040).</p>
<p>It has raised 5.82 trillion roubles by selling new tranches of six-month T-bills (series 22065 and 22060) making total proceeds from today's auctions 7.41 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
